==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|inh=1}}
{{etymon|de|id=to name|inh|gmh>nennen>to name|tree=1}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|nennen}}, {{m|gmh|nemmen}}, {{m|mgh|nemnen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|nemnen}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*namnijan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*namnijaną}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|hrx|nenne}}, {{cog|ang|nemnan}}, {{cog|enm|nemnen}}, {{cog|sv|nämna}}.
{{col-bottom}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈnɛnən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-nennen.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|nennen<nannte,genannt,nennte>}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[name]] (to give a name to)
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[call]], to [[describe]] {{+obj|de|acc<someone> + predicate&adjective/acc&noun<some name, title or description>}}
#: {{ux|de|'''Nennst''' du mich einen Dummkopf?|Are you '''calling''' me an idiot?}}
#: {{ux|de|Wir '''nennen''' den Hund Leo.|We '''call''' the dog Leo.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[mention]], to [[make known]], to [[tell]], to [[give]] {{+obj|de|dat<someone> + acc<some information>}}
#: {{ux|de|'''Nennen''' Sie mir den Ort des Treffens.|'''Tell''' me the location of the meeting.}}
#* {{quote-text|de|year=1918|author=w:de:Elisabeth von Heyking|chapter=s:de:Die Orgelpfeifen|title=Zwei Erzählungen|publisher=Phillipp Reclam jun.|pages=64–65
|passage=Namen '''wurden''' in diesen Berichten nicht '''genannt''', und in dieser Anonymität der Leistungen lag eine besondere entsagungsvolle Größe.|t=Names were not mentioned in these reports and in this anonymity of the achievements was a particular sacrificing greatness.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[say]], to [[speak]], to [[state]] (a name)
#: {{ux|de|Kannst du deinen Namen '''nennen'''?|Can you '''say''' your name?}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[call out]]; to [[give]] (e.g. some request)
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[be called]]; to be [[named]]; to go by some name

